     1	# NPM shim integrity manifest
     2	
     3	> **Integrity contract for the `ceo-orchestration` npm shim.** The package is
     4	> built and versioned (`VERSION` / `package.json`, currently 1.0.1).
     5	> Publishing stays gated — `npm-publish.yml` holds all `v*-rc.*` tags and
     6	> requires manual approval on GA tags via `environment: production-npm`.
     7	> The integrity controls enforced **today** are: (1) an `install.sh`
     8	> self-SHA tamper trailer (`# CEO-INSTALL-SHA256:`) that re-hashes the
     9	> installer at install time and **fails closed** on mismatch; (2) build
    10	> provenance via `npm publish --provenance` (`publishConfig.provenance:
    11	> true`, a Sigstore / SLSA-Level-2 attestation); and (3) a per-tarball
    12	> SHA-256 manifest (`npm/SHA256SUMS.txt` plus a detached `<tarball>.sha256`)
    13	> recorded by `npm-publish.yml` at tag cut. The sections below detail each
    14	> control and the items that remain release-operator steps (GPG detached
    15	> signature, reproducible build) rather than automated gates.
    16	
    17	## Contract
    18	
    19	Every release tarball (`npm pack --dry-run` output) MUST satisfy:
    20	
    21	| Control | Value / mechanism | Where enforced |
    22	|---|---|---|
    23	| SHA-256 manifest per file | `sha256sum` over every file in `files:` array | `.github/workflows/validate.yml` (to-add) + manifest committed to `npm/SHA256SUMS.txt` during release prep |
    24	| GPG detached signature | RFC 4880 signature over tarball | Release operator signs locally with project key; signature attached to GitHub Release as `ceo-orchestration-<version>.tgz.asc` |
    25	| SLSA Level-2 provenance | `npm publish --provenance` (Sigstore-attested via OIDC) | `.github/workflows/npm-publish.yml` already passes `--provenance`; requires `id-token: write` permission (already set) |
    26	| Reproducible build | `SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH` set to VERSION tag commit date | Release script (Sprint 17 scope) sets env var before `npm pack` |
    27	| Zero runtime dependencies | `Object.keys(dependencies).length === 0` | `.github/workflows/npm-publish.yml` step "Verify zero runtime dependencies" (existing) |
    28	| VERSION parity | `VERSION` file == `npm/package.json.version` == tag `v<version>` | `.github/workflows/npm-publish.yml` step "Verify VERSION matches tag" (existing) |
    29	
    30	## File-layer SHA-256 manifest (example)
    31	
    32	Generated during release prep, committed to `npm/SHA256SUMS.txt` adjacent to
    33	`package.json`:
    34	
    35	```
    36	<sha256>  bin/ceo-orch-init.js
    37	<sha256>  package.json
    38	<sha256>  scripts/install.sh
    39	<sha256>  templates/CLAUDE.md
    40	...
    41	```
    42	
    43	Consumers verify with:
    44	
    45	```bash
    46	cd $(npm root -g)/ceo-orchestration
    47	sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS.txt
    48	```
    49	
    50	## GPG key
    51	
    52	Project signing key fingerprint published in `docs/rotation-log.md` §NPM.
    53	Rotation: same 90-day maximum as other project credentials (ADR-040 §4).
    54	Public key distributed via GitHub Release notes + `.well-known/gpg.asc`.
    55	
    56	## SLSA Level-2 provenance
    57	
    58	`npm publish --provenance` attaches a Sigstore-signed attestation declaring:
    59	- Source repository (git URL)
    60	- Commit SHA
    61	- Workflow file that built the tarball
    62	- Builder (GitHub Actions runner identity)
    63	
    64	Consumers inspect via:
    65	
    66	```bash
    67	npm audit signatures ceo-orchestration
    68	```
    69	
    70	## Reproducible-build spec
    71	
    72	Inputs:
    73	- `SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH = <VERSION tag creator-date, unix-epoch>`
    74	- Node 20.x (SHA-pinned in `npm-publish.yml`)
    75	- No `npm install` for the bundle itself (zero runtime deps)
    76	
    77	Expected output: byte-identical tarball across any ubuntu-latest GitHub
    78	Actions runner with the same inputs. Deviation = rebuild failure.
    79	
    80	## CI verification (npm pack --dry-run assertion)
    81	
    82	A new step in `validate.yml` asserts:
    83	
    84	```yaml
    85	- name: Assert npm pack produces expected bundle
    86	  run: |
    87	    cd npm
    88	    SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH=$(git log -1 --format=%ct) npm pack --dry-run > /tmp/pack-out.txt
    89	    grep -q "^filename:" /tmp/pack-out.txt || { echo "::error::npm pack did not report filename"; exit 1; }
    90	```
    91	
    92	The `--dry-run` variant does not publish; it only asserts the pack step would
    93	succeed. Full tarball signing + provenance is the release-operator workflow.
    94	
    95	## Not yet automated (release-operator or out of scope)
    96	
    97	- **GPG detached signature** is a manual release-operator step (sign the
    98	  tarball locally; attach the `.asc` to the GitHub Release), not a CI gate.
    99	- **Reproducible build** (`SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH`-pinned `npm pack`) is specified
   100	  above but not yet asserted byte-for-byte in CI.
   101	- **SLSA Level-3** (hermetic build + two-party review) is out of scope; the
   102	  shipped provenance is SLSA Level-2 (`--provenance`).
