.claude/plans/PLAN-166/repass-rc3-cures/verdict-cures-round2.txt:3:Concrete failure scenario: the new adopter-facing text says fallback to root `VERSION` occurs “only when the marker is absent.” In reality, `check-framework-updates.sh` also falls back when the marker is present but unrecorded, malformed, or fails its delivery-record integrity check. An adopter with a pre-existing unrecorded marker therefore observes behavior contradicting the v1.3.0 release notes.
.claude/plans/PLAN-166/repass-rc3-cures/verdict-cures-round2.txt:5:Minimal fix: state that a well-formed marker is selected only when validated against its delivery record; otherwise root `VERSION` is used, retaining the documented sole-signal exception.
.claude/plans/PLAN-166/repass-rc3-cures/verdict-cures-round3.txt:4:   The new release note says both `install.sh` and `upgrade.sh` call `_ownership_verdict()`. They do not: all runtime call sites are in `scripts/upgrade.sh:1634`, `:1944`, and `:2107`. Install still decides locally through `INSTALL_ONE_WROTE` (`scripts/install.sh:1329`), marker delivery flags (`:1377`), and the pre-existing protocol early return (`:1883`). Thus P1-b is cured with a false architectural claim, and install can still diverge from the alleged single decision function.  
.claude/plans/PLAN-166/repass-rc3-cures/verdict-cures-round1.txt:21:   **Minimal fix:** after landing, always test the existing live workflow and fail if its marker or guard is absent; staged selection must be an explicit pre-landing mode, never an automatic fallback.
.claude/plans/PLAN-166/repass-rc3-cures/verdict-cures-round1.txt:24:   The adopter-facing cure is inaccurate. `_ownership_verdict()` consumes nine inputs; the tenth `fault` dimension is deliberately caller-side execution state. Also, the marker is not rewritten on every upgrade: skips, retargeted symlinks, unowned pre-existing markers, missing pinned-source markers, and failed backups preserve or omit it, with readers falling back to root `VERSION`.  
.claude/plans/PLAN-166/repass-rc3-cures/verdict-cures-round1.txt:25:   **Minimal fix:** describe the nine-input decision function plus caller-side fault axis, and qualify the marker as refreshed on successful framework-owned, unskipped upgrades and trusted marker-first only when delivery-recorded and integrity-valid.
.claude/plans/PLAN-166/repass-rc3-cures/verdict-cures-round1.txt:31:The remaining cures are correctly shaped: live counts are 166/27/190/68 excluding `__init__.py`, release/workflow counts are 31/22, the checklist marker site is real, RC publication remains excluded, and stable deleted/moved tags fail closed outside the split-snapshot race. YAML parsing, Bash syntax, Python 3.9 AST parsing, and `git diff --check` passed; full suites could not create temporary files in the read-only review sandbox.
