.claude/plans/PLAN-162/ceremony-2-staged/deny-write-twins.patch:33:   "_posture_keys_comment": "PLAN-163 T5.3/OQ5 — fail-closed posture keys (CC >=2.1.220). Key (1) permissions.defaultMode ships LIVE below (see _default_mode_arbitration_comment); the REMAINING keys ship COMMENTED for adopters. Dogfood status (2026-08-03): the framework repo enables workflowSizeGuideline and the sandbox keys; disableAutoMode was REMOVED from the dogfood settings by Owner decision (ceremony [SENT-PLAN165]) — beyond the documented no-mid-session-escalation effect it also strips 'auto' from the operator's native shift+tab mode cycle, and choosing the session mode is the operator's call, not the framework's. Adopters may still opt in. To adopt, add the keys literally: (2) top-level \"disableAutoMode\": \"disable\" — string enum whose sole value is 'disable' (the 2.1.220 schema rejects a boolean and SKIPS THE WHOLE settings file on mismatch — S286 live-fire); prevents automatic permission-mode escalation mid-session. (3) top-level \"workflowSizeGuideline\": <per your workflow scale; advisory sizing guideline for Workflow-tool fan-outs>. (4) \"sandbox\": { \"network\": { \"strictAllowlist\": true } } — tightens allowedDomains matching to the strict form. (5) \"sandbox\": { \"filesystem\": { \"disabled\": false } } — keeps filesystem confinement armed when the sandbox is enabled (true would fail-OPEN the FS layer). All keys are independent and additive; rollback is deleting the key. NEW-EVENT hook registrations (DirectoryAdded/Notification) are deliberately NOT in this template yet — T3.4 version-floor feature gate (upgrade.sh, default OFF), ADR-183 residual (e); this template stays at 45 registrations until the floor probe is recorded. This block is documentation only — underscore-prefixed keys are ignored by the harness.",
.claude/plans/PLAN-162/ceremony-2-staged/deny-write-twins.patch:34:   "_default_mode_arbitration_comment": "PLAN-163 T3.5/T5.3 ARBITRATION (CEO S284, ADR-183): permissions.defaultMode='manual' is a LIVE key in this template, not a commented posture option. Rationale: install.sh copies this file verbatim on a fresh install, and the U1 post-install oracle (test_upgrade_settings_migration.py TestU1TemplateParity) asserts the template already carries the T5.4 NEW baseline (defaultMode='manual', the 2.1.2xx rename of the ask-first permission mode — every non-allowlisted tool call prompts) — a commented-only defaultMode would red U1 and ship fresh installs on the OLD 'default' posture. Rollback: delete the defaultMode key (single-line revert; no hook consumes it — harness-level only).",
