     7	> The integrity controls enforced **today** are: (1) an `install.sh`
     8	> self-SHA tamper trailer (`# CEO-INSTALL-SHA256:`) that re-hashes the
     9	> installer at install time and **fails closed** on mismatch; (2) build
    10	> provenance via `npm publish --provenance` (`publishConfig.provenance:
    11	> true`, a Sigstore / SLSA-Level-2 attestation); and (3) a per-tarball
    12	> SHA-256 manifest (`npm/SHA256SUMS.txt` plus a detached `<tarball>.sha256`)
    13	> recorded by `npm-publish.yml` at tag cut. The sections below detail each
    14	> control and the items that remain release-operator steps (GPG detached
    15	> signature, reproducible build) rather than automated gates.
    16	
    17	## Contract
    18	
    19	Every release tarball (`npm pack --dry-run` output) MUST satisfy:
    20	
    21	| Control | Value / mechanism | Where enforced |
    22	|---|---|---|
    23	| SHA-256 manifest per file | `sha256sum` over every file in `files:` array | `.github/workflows/validate.yml` (to-add) + manifest committed to `npm/SHA256SUMS.txt` during release prep |
    24	| GPG detached signature | RFC 4880 signature over tarball | Release operator signs locally with project key; signature attached to GitHub Release as `ceo-orchestration-<version>.tgz.asc` |
    25	| SLSA Level-2 provenance | `npm publish --provenance` (Sigstore-attested via OIDC) | `.github/workflows/npm-publish.yml` already passes `--provenance`; requires `id-token: write` permission (already set) |
    26	| Reproducible build | `SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH` set to VERSION tag commit date | Release script (Sprint 17 scope) sets env var before `npm pack` |
    27	| Zero runtime dependencies | `Object.keys(dependencies).length === 0` | `.github/workflows/npm-publish.yml` step "Verify zero runtime dependencies" (existing) |
    28	| VERSION parity | `VERSION` file == `npm/package.json.version` == tag `v<version>` | `.github/workflows/npm-publish.yml` step "Verify VERSION matches tag" (existing) |
    29	
